{
  "id": "repeated_substring_pattern",
  "title": "Repeated Substring Pattern",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "String",
    "String Matching"
  ],
  "description": "<p>Given a string <code>s</code>, check if it can be constructed by taking a substring of it and appending multiple copies of the substring together.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> s = \"abab\"\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> It is the substring \"ab\" twice.\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> s = \"aba\"\n<strong>Output:</strong> false\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> s = \"abcabcabcabc\"\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> It is the substring \"abc\" four times or the substring \"abcabc\" twice.\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>1 &lt;= s.length &lt;= 10<sup>4</sup></code></li> <li><code>s</code> consists of lowercase English letters.</li> </ul>",
  "hints": [],
  "method": {
    "name": "repeatedSubstringPattern",
    "returnType": "auto",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "s",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
